==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]], [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]], [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] and [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]]

==Battleground==
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bakoo]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Bore]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**20 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
**1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Since the Bore spawns immediately, you should bring a cheaper Red crowd controller such as [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Enchantress Cat]]. Use some meatshields so you can start a stack of Enchantresses and once the Bore is perma-slowed, you won't need to spawn meatshields. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] or any other attackers that outrange Bore will easily take down the Bore at this point.

Once Bakoo spawns, you should try to lure the other enemies in order to separate them from Bakoo, since Bakoo has slow movement speed. If you take them out, Bakoo shouldn't be much of a problem because they have a high number of knockbacks, and hopefully won't be able to attack. Alternatively, if you have units with high piercing range, you won't have to kill the other enemies first for you to be able to repeatedly knockback Bakoo.

Alternatively,  if one has [[Evil Cat (Rare Cat)|Gentleman Bros.]], using Biobone or a good research up combo helps perma-freezing bore due to the extreme cheap cost and recharge time giving the chance of stacking LD cats, being a rare version of [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|ICat]] that can still demolish this stage.

